  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Every Christmas, Chef has a peculiar tradition of gifting a permutation PPP of length NNN. For each index iii in the permutation (1≤i≤N)(1 \\leq i \\leq N)(1≤i≤N), there is an associated value ViV_iVi​.\n\nThe value ViV_iVi​ is the number of steps needed to return to index iii when following this path:\n\n\nStart at index iii.\nLet the current index be kkk, then, move to the index PkP_kPk​.\nContinue until you return to index iii.\n\nFor example, let P=[3,2,5,4,1]P = [3, 2, 5, 4, 1]P=[3,2,5,4,1]. Then, at index 333, the path is 3→5→1→33 \\rightarrow 5 \\rightarrow 1 \\rightarrow 33→5→1→3, then V3=3V_3 = 3V3​=3.\nChef can perform operations to modify the permutation. In one operation, he can:\n\n\nSwap elements at positions iii and jjj.\nThe cost of this swap is Vi+VjV_i + V_jVi​+Vj​ (calculated before the swap).\nAfter the swap, values ViV_iVi​ and VjV_jVj​ (and possibly others) will change.\nChef's goal is to transform the permutation to achieve the maximum possible sum of all values (∑i=1NVi)(\\sum_{i=1}^N V_i)(∑i=1N​Vi​).\n\nFind the minimum total cost required to achieve the maximum possible sum of values.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the length of the permutation.\nThe next line contains NNN space separated integers PiP_iPi​, the elements of the permuation.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the minimum total cost required to achieve the maximum possible sum of values.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤Pi≤N;1 \\leq P_i \\leq N;1≤Pi​≤N; all values of PiP_iPi​ are distinct.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
