    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n2 3 1\n4\n4 1 3 2",
        "output": "0\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: It can be shown that the permutation already has maximum possible value sum. The value of each element is 333, resulting in a value sum of 999.\nTest case 222: For the initial permutation P=[4,1,3,2]P = [4, 1, 3, 2]P=[4,1,3,2], the value array is V=[3,3,1,3]V = [3, 3, 1, 3]V=[3,3,1,3].\nChef can swap indices 222 and 333 for a cost of 3+1=43 + 1 = 43+1=4, to obtain the permutation P=[4,3,1,2]P = [4, 3, 1, 2]P=[4,3,1,2], where value of each element is 444."
      }
    ]
